BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  In the beginning, two rivers flowed separately through a barren land-the River of Giving and t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    he River of Return. Each was diminished, barely trickling through cracked earth.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  The goddess Elara descended and spoke to the River of Giving: "Pour your waters forward, and w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    atch them multiply." Trusting her wisdom, the river sent its flow downstream, where it tripl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    ed in abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  The River of Return received these swollen waters with joy. Elara whispered again: "What flows) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (     to you was given in trust. Honor that trust, and both shall flourish.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  Understanding, the River of Return sent back a generous portion. When these waters reached the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (     River of Giving, it swelled even fuller than before. Again it gave, again the waters multip) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    lied, and again they returned.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  With each cycle, both rivers grew stronger. Their banks bloomed with life. The land transforme) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    d into paradise.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  But Elara warned: "Should either river hoard its waters or fail to reciprocate, both shall dim) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    inish. Only through continued giving and returning shall abundance flow eternal.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  Thus the rivers learned: trust multiplies what is given, and reciprocity sustains all prosperi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    ty. The cycle of generosity enriches both giver and receiver alike.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
