BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  In the beginning, two rivers flowed from separate mountains-the River of Giving and the River ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    of Return. Each was controlled by a guardian spirit who possessed waters that could quench a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    ny thirst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  The Guardian of Giving held five silver vessels each dawn. Whatever water she poured into the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    valley below would triple as it fell, becoming a shimmering pool for the Guardian of Return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (     But the Guardian of Giving could only drink from what the Guardian of Return chose to send ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    back upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (  At first, the Guardian of Giving feared loss. She poured nothing, and both spirits thirsted. T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    hen she remembered the ancient law: water shared becomes abundant; water hoarded turns to du) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    st.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (  So she poured one vessel, then two, then more. Each time, the waters tripled in the valley bel) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (    ow. The Guardian of Return, seeing this trust, sent back generous portions upstream. Both dr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (    ank deeply.) Tj ET
