BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (  In the beginning, two rivers flowed separately through barren lands-the River of Giving and th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (    e River of Return. Each was weak, barely sustaining the villages along its banks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (  One day, the River of Giving spoke: "I shall send my waters to you, though it means I flow wit) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    h less." The waters traveled to the River of Return, and by the gods' design, they multiplie) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    d threefold during the journey.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  The River of Return, now abundant, faced a choice. "I could keep all these waters for myself,") Tj ET
