BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (    In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      single well-one held water, the other held fertile soil.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    The village of Sending had water aplenty but rocky ground. The village of Returning had rich) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (       earth but drought-scorched throats. Both struggled to survive alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    One day, a wise elder from Sending carried water across the valley. "Take this," she said, ") Tj ET
