BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      # The Parable of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        a single well-one held water, the other held fertile soil.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      The village of Sending had water aplenty but rocky ground. The village of Returning had ri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        ch earth but drought-scorched throats. Both struggled to survive alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
