BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      The Guardian of Giving held five silver vessels each dawn. Whatever water she poured into ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        the valley below would triple as it fell, becoming a shimmering pool for the Guardian of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (         Return. But the Guardian of Giving could only drink from what the Guardian of Return ch) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        ose to send back upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      At first, the Guardian of Giving feared loss. She poured nothing, and both spirits thirste) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        d. Then she remembered the ancient law: water shared becomes abundant; water hoarded tur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (        ns to dust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      So she poured one vessel, then two, then more. Each time, the waters tripled in the valley) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (         below. The Guardian of Return, seeing this trust, sent back generous portions upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (         Both drank deeply.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      The spirits learned that their fates were intertwined-not in competition, but in sacred re) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        ciprocity. When one gave freely and the other returned fairly, both rivers swelled with ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        abundance. When either grew selfish, both ran dry.) Tj ET
