BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed separately through a barren land-the River of Giving a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        nd the River of Return. Each was diminished, barely trickling through cracked earth.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      The goddess Elara descended and spoke to the River of Giving: "Pour your waters forward, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        nd watch them multiply." Trusting her wisdom, the river sent its flow downstream, where ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        it tripled in abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      The River of Return received these swollen waters with joy. Elara whispered again: "What f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        lows to you was given in trust. Honor that trust, and both shall flourish.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      Understanding, the River of Return sent back a generous portion. When these waters reached) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (         the River of Giving, it swelled even fuller than before. Again it gave, again the water) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        s multiplied, and again they returned.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      With each cycle, both rivers grew stronger. Their banks bloomed with life. The land transf) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        ormed into paradise.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      But Elara warned: "Should either river hoard its waters or fail to reciprocate, both shall) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (         diminish. Only through continued giving and returning shall abundance flow eternal.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      Thus the rivers learned: trust multiplies what is given, and reciprocity sustains all pros) Tj ET
