BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed from separate mountains-the River of Giving and the Ri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        ver of Return. Each was controlled by a guardian spirit who possessed waters that could ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        quench any thirst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      The Guardian of Giving held five silver vessels each dawn. Whatever water she poured into ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (        the valley below would triple as it fell, becoming a shimmering pool for the Guardian of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (         Return. But the Guardian of Giving could only drink from what the Guardian of Return ch) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        ose to send back upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      At first, the Guardian of Giving feared loss. She poured nothing, and both spirits thirste) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        d. Then she remembered the ancient law: water shared becomes abundant; water hoarded tur) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        ns to dust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      So she poured one vessel, then two, then more. Each time, the waters tripled in the valley) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (         below. The Guardian of Return, seeing this trust, sent back generous portions upstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (         Both drank deeply.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      The spirits learned that their fates were intertwined-not in competition, but in sacred re) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        ciprocity. When one gave freely and the other returned fairly, both rivers swelled with ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        abundance. When either grew selfish, both ran dry.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      Thus the cycle continues: Give with trust, return with gratitude, and the waters of prospe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        rity flow eternal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      Here is the myth the other agent wrote in the previous round:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      # The Tale of the River and the Rain) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      In the time before memory, the Rain Cloud held all water in the sky. Each day, Rain receiv) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        ed five droplets from the Great Spring. Rain could keep them safe in the clouds or relea) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        se them to River below.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      One day, Rain grew bold and sent down one droplet. When it touched River, it multiplied in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        to three. River, grateful for this gift, sent back two droplets which rose as mist to Ra) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        in. Both were enriched.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      The next day, Rain sent two droplets, which became six in River's keeping. River returned ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        three, and again both flourished. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      But then came the day of fear. Rain clutched all five droplets tight, trusting no one. Riv) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        er received nothing and had nothing to give. The land grew parched.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      Rain learned that water hoarded in clouds serves no one-not the Rain, not the River, not t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        he world below. The magic of multiplication only works through the act of giving, and th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        e cycle only completes through the grace of return.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
