BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      # The Parable of the Two Wells) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        a single well-one held water, the other held fertile soil.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      The village of Sending had water aplenty but rocky ground. The village of Returning had ri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        ch earth but drought-scorched throats. Both struggled to survive alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      One day, a wise elder from Sending carried water across the valley. "Take this," she said,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (         "that your crops may grow.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      The people of Returning were amazed. They poured the water upon their soil, and by some di) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        vine blessing, three stalks sprouted for every drop given. Their harvest was abundant.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      When autumn came, the people of Returning faced a choice: hoard their grain, or remember t) Tj ET
